    {
      "title": "Rahul Gandhi says India has become a 'side player' in global affairs",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/rahul-gandhi-says-india-has-become-a-side-player-in-global-affairs-126111901112_1.html",
      "description": "India always had a sophisticated understanding of geopolitics, but has become a side player in global affairs, Congress leader Rahul Gandhi has said, citing the role Pakistan played in negotiating peace between the US and Iran.\n\"India, by its size, naturally has a global voice and India should be actively involved in global conversations. But frankly, India has become a side player,\" Gandhi said during an interaction with students at the University of Chicago on Wednesday.\nGandhi, the Leader of the Opposition in the Lok Sabha, said India has relationships with the US, Iran and Russia. \"I'm pretty shocked that Pakistan is busy negotiating with the Iranians and the Americans, and India's just looking,\" he said.\nHe said that soon after Independence, India was the leader of the Non-Aligned Movement, which gave it a certain stature in the world, and he would love New Delhi to regain that voice on the global stage.\nGandhi also slammed the foreign policy pursued by Prime Minister Narendra",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-20T03:54:21"
    }
